                <pb facs="0336" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg240"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2 in No. 91.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Tsung-li Yamên to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November 8,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 24.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: The Yamên has the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your excellency’s communication of the 3d instant,
                    wherein you stated that you were bringing to Peking a legation escort of 20 men;
                    that they would be ready to leave Tientsin in the morning of the 5th instant,
                    and you therefore requested that the Yamen have arranged for them such train
                    accommodation and provide such military escort as has been done for the guards
                    of the other legations.</p>
                <p>Upon receipt of your excellency’s communication the Yamên telegraphed, on the 4th
                    instant, to the superintendent of northern trade to instruct his subordinates to
                    take proper care and the governor of Peking was also instructed to have suitable
                    train accommodations furnished the escort.</p>
                <p>A necessary reply to your excellency’s communication.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
